# tools/cr/crypto_shake_witness.rish — SHAKE128 and SHAKE256, the SHA-3 extendable-output functions, authored in pure Rye as a composition
# over the GREEN Keccak-f[1600] sponge in crypto/sha3.rye: the same permutation and pad10*1 rule, the 0x1f domain delimiter, and a squeeze
# that walks across as many rate-sized blocks as the output needs, proven against the canonical SHAKE known-answers and Zig's independent
# std.crypto Shake128/Shake256 across both the absorb and the squeeze block edges (Season G · Cryptography).
#
# Season: crypto — Season G's extendable-output stone, beside crypto/sha3.rye and crypto/keccak256.rye. This rung authors NO new
# cryptography: it composes one already-GREEN stone — the Keccak-f[1600] permutation and sponge proven in crypto/sha3.rye against FIPS 202
# and std.crypto — passing it the 0x1f SHAKE delimiter and asking for an arbitrary output length. The decisive extension it earns from the
# sibling is the sponge's generality: the squeeze now emits rate bytes, permutes, and reads again, so multi-block output is proven, not just
# the first block. That generality opens SHA3-224/384, cSHAKE, KMAC, and the post-quantum XOFs (SHAKE256 inside Ed448 and SPHINCS+, SHAKE128
# seeding ML-KEM and ML-DSA matrices) as later rungs.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-175524_rye-first-crypto-parity-and-the-decision-wave.md (the wave that seats the Rye-first spine).
# Clean-room: the 0x1f delimiter, the two SHAKE rates, and the sponge law are the public FIPS 202 standard's own; the arithmetic is our GREEN
# sha3.rye, never a copied line (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# crypto/shake.rye calls the proven sponge with rate 168 (SHAKE128) or 136 (SHAKE256) and the 0x1f delimiter, squeezing out.len bytes across
# as many permute-and-read blocks as the output spans. Parity is proven at selftest against the canonical SHAKE128("")→32B and
# SHAKE256("")→64B known-answers, and Zig's own std.crypto Shake128/Shake256 byte-for-byte across the absorb padding edges (rate-1, exact-rate,
# rate+1) AND the squeeze block edges (outputs of 504 and 408 bytes span three rate blocks). The XOF prefix property holds, and the bounds
# refuse an over-long message and a zero-or-oversize output before any work. Purely local — no key, no network, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/cr/crypto_shake_witness.rish

say "crypto-shake: Language EN — SHAKE128 and SHAKE256 are the SHA-3 extendable-output functions: where SHA3-256/512 read a fixed digest, a SHAKE reads as many bytes as the caller asks for. They are the XOF stone the modern and post-quantum world stands on — SHAKE256 inside Ed448 and SPHINCS+, SHAKE128 seeding ML-KEM (Kyber) and ML-DSA (Dilithium) matrices, and cSHAKE/KMAC/TupleHash all build on this squeeze."
say "crypto-shake: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: call the sponge crypto/sha3.rye already proved on metal with rate 168 (SHAKE128) or 136 (SHAKE256) and the 0x1f delimiter, then squeeze rate bytes, permute, and read again for as many blocks as the output spans. This rung authors no permutation of its own; it earns from the sibling one decisive extension — the sponge's extendable-output generality."
say "crypto-shake: Lens TAME — no new cryptography: the permutation, absorb, and squeeze are the GREEN crypto/sha3.rye, proven byte-for-byte against FIPS 202 and std.crypto. Bounded input (max_message_bytes) and bounded output (max_output_bytes), contract asserts on every function. Parity holds against the canonical SHAKE known-answers AND Zig's independent std.crypto Shake128/Shake256 across both the absorb padding edges and the squeeze block edges — outputs of 504 and 408 bytes span three rate blocks, so multi-block squeeze is proven; the bounds refuse an over-long message and a zero-or-oversize output before any work. Purely local — no key, no network, no funds, no device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "crypto/bin/shake"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p crypto/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build crypto/shake.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "crypto-shake: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "crypto/bin/shake.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "crypto-shake: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "crypto-shake: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN crypto-shake' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "crypto-shake: selftest did not print the GREEN crypto-shake line"
